data.content:
Build succeeds. Here's what was created:

**`Components/ScreenSize.cs`** — enum with `Mobile`, `Tablet`, `Desktop` values.

**`Components/ScreenSizeProvider.razor`** — wraps `ChildContent` in a `<CascadingValue>` of type `ScreenSize`. Defaults to `Desktop`, then calls JS on first render to get the actual width and listen for resize events.

**`wwwroot/screenSize.js`** — JS module that reports `window.innerWidth` on init and on every `resize` event via `[JSInvokable]` callback.

**Usage in child components:**
```razor
@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public ScreenSize ScreenSize { get; set; }
}
```

The component requires **interactive rendering** (Server or WebAssembly) since it uses JS interop. Wrap your content with `<ScreenSizeProvider>` and any descendant can read the cascading `ScreenSize` value that updates in real time on resize.
